v class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688070-arindhal-the-wind-lords?p=712219#post712219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup, only thing more amazing are sharks really. And second ed is dying for a reiterating of the rokea, not those terrible brine born lol</div> </div> </div> </div>A wolf with eagles wings, gills and jaws and sensory organs of a shark added to it. Just give it a pick-up truck and a gun and you have the perfect hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T12:01:13-07:00","id":712810,"title":"","content":"Loved it. I don't like the fera much, but I like the idea of things similar to the uratha hidden and in small number, specially in different eras of the game.<br /> <br /> For instance, when Dark Eras is released I intend to adapt the Aztec Skinchangers scenario and try to build a playable jaguar race similar to the Uratha (using whatever the skinchangers get as a base). Something regional, and that is extinct nowadays. Or I plan to use it if someone else does it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But seeing this, I have another idea as well. If I get to play Forsaken by Rome, I think this would be a great antagonist/rival.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T13:28:44-07:00","id":712956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Max Deltree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688070-arindhal-the-wind-lords?p=712810#post712810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loved it. I don't like the fera much, but I like the idea of things similar to the uratha hidden and in small number, specially in different eras of the game.<br /> <br /> For instance, when Dark Eras is released I intend to adapt the Aztec Skinchangers scenario and try to build a playable jaguar race similar to the Uratha (using whatever the skinchangers get as a base). Something regional, and that is extinct nowadays. Or I plan to use it if someone else does it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But seeing this, I have another idea as well. If I get to play Forsaken by Rome, I think this would be a great antagonist/rival.</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially with the symbolism of the Eagle in Antiquity. Furthermore, in the H:tV 1e book &quot;Spirit Slayers&quot;, there was a barbarian tribe that was almost exclusively werewolves and their wolf-blooded, and they were antagonists/sometimes-allies of Rome. Perhaps the Eagle symbolism was inspired by heavy-handed influence from secret Wind-Lord elite, who clashed with this tribe and a number of others who were heavily wolf-populated, arguing/sometimes getting in bed with the vampiric Camarilla in order to direct conquesting expansion towards the tribes' many territories....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T13:50:33-07:00","id":712982,"title":"","content":"The Pure book has an Ivory Claws lodge that dates back to Roman days, if not before, called the Council of Eagles. They were sort of like a self-appointed secret police, punishing werewolves for bad behavior. Perhaps they were originally allies with the Arindhal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T14:49:58-07:00","id":713058,"title":"","content":"This is pretty awesome Claire.<br /> <br /> Though, hopefully pertinent question: would the Arindhal even carry the risk of Kuruth? The Uratha supposedly inherited the Rage and its power from Urfarah. The terror and indomitable healing of their Killing Form comes from it, among other things, and I don't see a link to a close equivalent in the ancestry of the Wind-Lords.<br /> <br /> Perhaps they would be better served by having something different of comparable significance? I don't think the theme of rage as written for Werewolves lends itself to their image based on what you wrote so far or the symbolism and qualities commonly associated with eagles. Granted, it depends on your vision for<i> their</i> themes, so maybe the thought comes prematurely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 10-21-2015, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T15:26:28-07:00","id":713096,"title":"","content":"Wasn't the Rage part of the curse from Luna?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T15:35:57-07:00","id":713101,"title":"","content":"Was it? I don't remember anything in the Second Edition core or any of the first edition material I read (which was admittedly sparse) suggesting that.<br /> <br /> (But that doesn't particularly make the Rage seem fitting for the Arindhal either.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T15:49:59-07:00","id":713129,"title":"","content":"Consider it the Zeal of Helios. You could even change it to &quot;Zeal&quot; if that fits better. The Arindhal in their war-form are not slavering, roaring beasts. They're like the cold light of dawn. They act with such singular focus\u2014the act of killing\u2014that all else ceases to matter. It's like the vision of an eagle but with complete tunnel-vision. <i>Kill. Purge. Prey. </i>Focused as a ray of sunlight, searing like the surface of the sun, bearer of Helios' manifest wrath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T16:12:33-07:00","id":713149,"title":"","content":"That works! Though I personally still feel like that differs from the Rage enough in spirit(snerk) that adjusted mechanics for triggering kuruth might be justified. Which... isn't all that helpful as feedback when I have no discrete suggestions on how to do it, I realize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T16:30:28-07:00","id":713176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688070-arindhal-the-wind-lords?p=713149#post713149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That works! Though I personally still feel like that differs from the Rage enough in spirit(snerk) that adjusted mechanics for triggering kuruth might be justified. Which... isn't all that helpful as feedback when I have no discrete suggestions on how to do it, I realize.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still a form of Rage. The Arindhal operate on Tranquil Fury vs. Roaring Rampage of Revenge-style beatdown. Both are forms of anger, and both manifest with some sort of killing instinct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T17:02:21-07:00","id":713207,"title":"","content":"I understand the concept, I just think it has potential to be more meaningful if it was taken in a somewhat distinct direction. I still think it does well as is mind, and Zeal is nice fluff for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T22:12:03-07:00","id":713700,"title":"","content":"To make things different than Kuruth, maybe Zeal makes character to strive to engage in making Tilts with every thier attack. With classical &quot;Not in the eyes!&quot; plead of their enemies?<br /> <br /> Kuruth makes you attack - Zeal makes you go with the grace. Other ideas - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/691663-kun-shulor\">Kun-shulor<br /> ( Weresquides )</a> have Hunger Rage to eat brains. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-22-2015, 01